      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The shift away from globalism is a rational response to current geopolitical tensions, and protectionist trade policies are a logical way for countries to secure their interests. By imposing tariffs and quotas, countries can level the playing field against unfair trade practices, protect domestic industries, and safeguard national security. This approach has been successfully employed by countries like the US, Japan, and South Korea, which have used protectionism to boost their economies and assert their influence on the world stage.",
      "source": "target",
